%I A397685 #11 Jul 26 2026 22:23:42
%S A397685 672,143573364313605309726720,352338107624535891640320,
%T A397685 48949643430560436794021629524876790263031553747866371344635527168
%N A397685 Multiperfect numbers k that are divisible by some 2^m but not by 2^(m+1)-1.
%C A397685 First term is 3-perfect, the rest are known to be 5-perfects. In order for every single currently known k-perfect number here to be divisible by 2^(m+1)-1, it has to be multiplied by k.
%C A397685 All odd multiperfects are not terms of this sequence as 2^0=2^1-1.
%e A397685 672 is divisible by 2^5 but not by 2^6-1. Hence, 672 is in this sequence.
%Y A397685 Cf. A000203, A005820, A046060, A007691.
